Subject: [PATCH] modelblaster: integer lowering of a frozen quantisation plan -- int16, per-channel scales, split dispatches

iiswc-tutorial ROCC_DECOUPLED.md 8.13 chose, in float simulation (fq.py / quant_fix.py), the
Moonshine encoder quantisations that transcribe: an int16 stem, per-channel residual adds,
rows on o_proj/fc2, and either a split multi-range stem for today's int8-by-int8 engine ("R")
or per-row int16-by-int8 convolutions for a width-selectable one ("F3PR").  This patch makes
those plans code-generate, with an INTEGER golden, so the generated C (and nothing simulated)
is what gets measured.  OPT-IN: nothing changes unless pipeline/extract_q16.py is invoked;
every existing IR extracts and code-generates byte-identically.

1. pipeline/extract_q16.py (new).  `python -m modelblaster.pipeline.extract_q16 --model M
   --plan PLAN.json --out-dir DIR`.  A plan (iiswc-tutorial moonshine/q16_plan.py) is
   quant_fix.build()'s decision frozen as JSON: per tensor pt int8/int16, pc int8 or
   multi-range int8; per weight pt, per-row or row groups; weight rows a_c.  extract_int8
   runs UNCHANGED on the plan's ranges over the model with the rows applied, then the ops the
   plan changes are rewritten and the golden is simulated op by op in integers (stock kinds
   exactly as MB_INT8_GOLDEN_C_FLOAT=1 simulates them).  MB_INT8_DUMP_ACTIVATIONS honoured.
     conv2d_s8, multi-range output   split16_s8 hi/lo + 2*G*R stock conv2d_s8 + mrcombine_s16
     conv2d_s8, int16, per-row       conv2d_s16_pc
     tanh_s8 / gelu_s8 on int16      lut16_s16, lut16_pc_s8 (65,536-entry tables, float64)
     groupnorm_s8 on int16           groupnorm_s16
     permute4_s8 on int16            permute4_s16
     add_s8, per-channel output      add_pc_s8, add_s16_pc_s8
     layernorm_s8, pc / int16 input  layernorm_pc_s8, layernorm_s16_s8
     linear_s8, per-row weights      linear_s8_pc (stock)
   Per-channel scales ride in tensor metadata (quant.scale_pc, quant.axis) through
   view/permute.
   THE SPLIT: hi = min((x + 128) >> 8, 127), lo = clamp8(x - 256*hi), bias in the L dispatch.
   The offset split hi = x >> 8, lo = (x & 0xFF) - 128 was measured and rejected: a small
   negative x gives hi = -1, H and L then carry +-256*sum(w) each and saturate in the fine
   range (float simulation of the split composition, dev-clean 765 utterances: R 28.6 % WER
   against 8.45 % with this split; fq.py's ideal 8.31 %).  Bias in H was also worse (its step
   is 256*s_in*sw_g, ~2 output codes on conv3).
   THE NORMALISATIONS share one exact core: S, Q = sums (128-bit), V = K*Q - S^2 + eps_q,
   R = isqrt(floor(2^120 / V)), t = (K*u - S)*R >> 44, out = (t*g + b*2^16 + 2^31) >> 32.
2. pipeline/extract_graph.py: extract_int8(range_overrides=None) -- the plan's ranges replace
   calibration's for the tensors it names.  None = stock.
3. pipeline/generate_skeleton.py: IR dtype "i16" (int16_t) for buffers and inputs, int16
   weight arrays, and the call emitters of the eleven new kinds.
4. pipeline/reference_kernels.py: KernelSpecs for the eleven kinds, each reference being its
   integer golden (no float anywhere; 128-bit division is libgcc's __udivti3), and curated
   pext_nl candidates, BIT_EXACT, whose sources live in iiswc-tutorial
   fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kernels/pext_nl/:
     add_pc_s8 / add_s16_pc_s8   pext_int_block    channel blocks, no divide per element
     mrcombine_s16               pext_fine_first   finest range first, early exit
     groupnorm_s16               pext_int_memo     t tabulated per sample over its code span
     conv2d_s16_pc               pext_split_dot8   exact 256*hi + lo + 128 taps, MBP.DOT8
   (split16_s8, lut16_*, layernorm_*, permute4_s16 take the reference.)

Checked (iiswc-tutorial fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/moonshine/q16_gates.py, q16_gates_*.json):
  * reference C vs the integer golden at every dispatch: R 159/159, R3 207/207, F3PR 129/129;
  * curated new kinds with reference stock kinds, every dispatch: same counts, all exact;
  * q16_stress.c: 373,306 cases at -O2 and 37,303 under ASan+UBSan, 0 mismatches;
  * rv64imac objects: 0 soft-float, 0 libm;
  * attn_block, dronet, ffn_block, kws_cnn, kws_digit_ctc_t, lenet, norm_block, moonshine_enc:
    graph.json/io.npz/weights.npz identical with and without this patch; moonshine_enc's
    generated C identical for --target pext_nl and roccmoon.

Applies on top of patches/0009, 0020, 0060, 0070, 0100, 0102 and 0104.

